"""Round 7-only assessment. Run from the project root after audit_r7_extension.R."""
import csv
from pathlib import Path
from html import escape
out=Path('temp/r7_extension_reassessment')
def read(n):
    with (out/n).open() as f:return list(csv.DictReader(f))
def table(rows,cols=None):
    cols=cols or list(rows[0]);return '<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr>'+''.join('<th>'+escape(c)+'</th>' for c in cols)+'</tr></thead><tbody>'+''.join('<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+escape(str(r.get(c,'')))+'</td>' for c in cols)+'</tr>' for r in rows)+'</tbody></table></div>'
parts=[]
def sec(h,t):parts.append('<h2>'+h+'</h2>'+t)
counts=read('candidate_estimation_counts.csv')
main=[r for r in counts if r['cohort']=='oc' and r['mode']=='in_person' and r['window']=='annual']
weekly=[r for r in counts if r['cohort']=='oc' and r['window']=='weekly_job' and r['group']=='non_Addis' and r['specification'] in ['historical_controls','common_current_hh_food']]
controls=[r for r in read('control_coverage.csv') if r['cohort']=='oc' and r['variable'] in ['fdsec00r7','electr7','wallr7','roofr7','floorr7','flcookr7','constructed:hhsize','constructed:wi','constructed:hq','constructed:cd','constructed:elecq','constructed:foodsec']]
sec('Conclusion and recommended design','''<div class="finding"><p><strong>A Round 7 annual-employment extension with contemporaneous household controls is feasible for in-person respondents.</strong> Historical treatment, instrument and childhood controls can be linked from earlier rounds as in the original analysis. The annual outcome has a substantially stronger comparability basis than the earlier joint R6/R7 assessment established.</p></div>
<p>For the primary older-cohort analysis, use R7 in-person annual main-activity salary/wage outcomes and R7 household size, wealth components and electricity. Retain R1 childhood/caregiver/land controls and the original treatment/policy assignment. A separate common-weekly-outcome exercise can include phone respondents using controls genuinely available in both modes. R6 is deferred and plays no role in this assessment.</p>
<p>The audit constructs aggregate candidate sample counts, not fitted estimates or production datasets. The old R1–R5 results and sample definitions are preserved. Remaining construction checks concern R7 index provenance, routing and sample diagnostics, not the absence of a fresh childhood measurement.</p>''')
sec('Annual outcome comparability is confirmed by the questionnaires','''<p><strong>R5 activity 1 was intended to be the most important annual activity by time spent.</strong> The original R5 Ethiopia questionnaire, employment section 5.2 (PDF page 36), explicitly instructs respondents to list their three annual activities by time spent, beginning with the most important. The current script selects ACTIDR5=1. R7 section 9.3.1 likewise asks for the most-time paid or unpaid activity over the past 12 months.</p>
<p>This resolves the earlier report’s uncertainty about first-listed versus most-time activity selection. Both use an annual reference period and include paid and unpaid work. The data collection changed from a ranked list to a single main-activity module, so reporting differences remain possible, but the intended selection rule is aligned.</p>
<p>In the R7 older-cohort full interviews, all 451 respondents answering yes to at least one annual work screen have a valid annual activity code. The other 181 answer no to all three annual screens. There are no unexplained missing annual activity types among those screened as working. In the younger cohort, the corresponding counts are 910 annual workers and 496 nonworkers.</p>
<p>Use salary code 13 and wage codes 5/12/13, retaining the original different exclusions and denominators. Confirm code labels source by source: in the actual R5 ACTR5 and R7 raw fields, 19 is housemaid and 20 is other non-agriculture; generic guide lists should not override archived variable labels. R7 additionally labels 21 as crop self-employment and 22 as livestock self-employment; the audit maps these to legacy categories 1 and 4 for denominator consistency. No such 21/22 observations occur in the OC annual file, but they occur in the YC file.</p>
<p>Known annual nonworkers are assigned zero; unknown screens or an unknown worker activity remain missing. A missing activity type is never itself evidence of no work. R7 pre-fills the annual section when the weekly/current job is confirmed to be the same; the observed complete annual activity coverage is checked rather than assuming all raw blanks are ordinary nonresponse.</p>'''+table(read('outcome_coverage.csv')))
sec('Contemporaneous controls: what can be updated','''<p>The original regression’s nutrition and caregiver variables were historical already. Their absence from a fresh R7 questionnaire does not block the extension. Distinguish them from the household measures that can be updated to the R7 interview date.</p>'''+table([
{'control':'Household size','in_person':'Reconstruct from current roster','phone':'Reconstruct from current roster','decision':'Count livhser7=1, include index participant; require roster completion. Constructed hhsize is entirely missing in R7.'},
{'control':'Housing quality, wealth','in_person':'Raw walls/roof/floor/rooms, asset and service material present; constructed wi/hq available','phone':'No corresponding housing/assets battery in the short raw questionnaire','decision':'Use definition-aligned R7 indices for in-person primary analysis after raw-component checks. Do not treat phone constructed values as proven contemporaneous.'},
{'control':'Consumer durables','in_person':'Raw assets and constructed cd present','phone':'Constructed cd exists but no matching complete asset module inspected','decision':'In-person current CD feasible; retain historical CD in a common-mode sensitivity until phone provenance is verified.'},
{'control':'Electricity','in_person':'electr7 directly observed for all 632 OC records','phone':'No electr7 in short core; constructed elecq populated','decision':'Use current raw/constructed agreement in person. Do not substitute utility-disruption questions for electricity access.'},
{'control':'Food situation','in_person':'fdsec00r7 observed for all 632','phone':'fdsec00r7 observed for all 64','decision':'Current four-category food situation feasible in both modes; report it as a deliberate replacement for historic foodsec_r3 if adopted.'},
{'control':'Land/house ownership','in_person':'ownhser7 is house ownership','phone':'Short module lacks equivalent housing battery','decision':'Retain R1 land-under-house ownership control. Current house ownership is not the same construct.'},
{'control':'Region/rurality','in_person':'Current region and location metadata available','phone':'Use verified residence metadata, not work-region field','decision':'Keep historical policy geography for E_is and inference; label current residence separately.'},
{'control':'Childhood/caregiver/background','in_person':'Historical source permitted','phone':'Historical source permitted','decision':'Keep original nutrition, caregiver, language, ethnicity and other fixed controls; do not replace them with adult measures.'},
]))
sec('Wealth-index definition alignment matters','''<p>The correct source-name bridge is easy to miss: <strong>legacy wi_new/hq_new are closer to the new release’s wi/hq (without _new)</strong> if the goal is the old wall-material definition. In R5, the legacy wi_new and hq_new each match their un-suffixed new-release counterpart on all 2,613 paired observed records. The new release’s wi_new/hq_new instead incorporate concrete blocks as good-quality walls.</p>
<p>Thus the primary consistent-definition contemporary-control audit uses R7 wi and hq, mapping them to clearly named R7 analysis variables; it does not copy the latest _new indices merely because the legacy controls also had that suffix. Report the revised concrete-block variant as a sensitivity if desired.</p>
<p>The index identity wi=(hq+sv+cd)/3 holds on all observed OC in-person index records. This validates internal arithmetic, not the full material/asset construction. Before final estimation, verify the room-per-person denominator, wall/roof/floor code crosswalk and durables item set against raw R7 sources and the legacy methodology. A successful R5 numerical bridge does not replace those R7 checks.</p>'''+table(read('legacy_index_definition_bridge.csv'))+table(read('index_provenance_checks.csv')))
sec('Household size requires reconstruction, not dropping the control','''<p>The constructed R7 hhsize column has no observations in either cohort or mode. The raw household rosters are present and distinguish current members from people who moved, died or are no longer known. Counting every roster row would substantially overstate household size.</p>
<p>The candidate audit counts only livhser7=1, checks unique childcode/member-ID pairs, includes the participant (member ID 0), and retains a size only when the core cmplthhr7 completion flag is yes. This yields observed household sizes for 626 of 632 OC in-person records and all 64 OC phone records. Incomplete rosters remain missing; they are not treated as zero-member households.</p>'''+table(read('roster_reconstruction_check.csv')))
sec('Phone respondents: distinguish actual current data from populated columns','''<p>There are 64 OC and 129 YC phone records in the archived core, disjoint from the in-person sample. Annual participation screens are present, but annual main-activity-type detail is absent. All 53 OC phone annual workers therefore lack the annual job type needed for a comparable annual salary/wage classification. The audit does not build an annual outcome using just the 11 phone nonworkers; that would select on employment status.</p>
<p>Weekly/current job types are available for phone respondents. The weekly module also includes temporarily absent current jobs, so its salary/wage outcome is not simply an indicator for physically working last week. The audit distinguishes known no-current-job/nonwork routes from job-type records and validates the screening skips. Annual and weekly outcomes are kept separate.</p>
<p><strong>Constructed phone index provenance remains unverified.</strong> All 64 OC phone records contain constructed wealth/housing/service indices and electricity, despite no matching current housing/assets/electricity battery in their short raw core or household roster. YC phone records have no constructed wi/hq but do have cd/electricity. These are genuine observations about the files, not grounds for declaring the fields either fabricated or contemporaneous. The OC phone values are not merely identical copies of all legacy R5 values, so simple R5 carry-forward does not explain them either.</p>
<p>Accordingly, the audit deliberately treats those unverified phone wealth/electricity measures as unusable for the full contemporaneous-control specification. Zero candidate cases in that specification are a provenance-based design restriction, not a claim that the constructed values are numerically missing. A common-mode alternative updates household size and food situation while retaining historical wealth/electricity controls. Phone mode is concentrated in conflict-affected Amhara areas, so annual in-person-only estimates need a clearly stated geographic/mode coverage limitation.</p>'''+table(controls,['mode','variable','present','observed','non_special']))
sec('Candidate estimation samples: older cohort','''<p>These counts link R7 respondents to the existing legacy analysis files, keep the existing nonzero/nonmissing R4 language-score eligibility condition, retain historical IMTI/E_is and childhood controls, and apply the original outcome-specific exclusions. No balanced-panel requirement is imposed. Policy-region grouping remains the original historical grouping.</p>
<p>Specifications are: historical_controls (all original controls); r7_household_controls (replace hhsize, wealth, housing quality, CD and electricity with verified R7 counterparts); r7_household_plus_food (also use current four-category food situation); common_current_hh_food (update only size and food, retaining historical wealth/electricity to allow phone inclusion). Addis-specific counts also require the original entype_r4 control.</p>
<p><strong>The primary annual, in-person, non-Addis counts are 352 salary and 266 wage complete cases with contemporaneous household controls</strong>, compared with 358 and 271 when retaining all historical controls. Updating food situation as well leaves these counts unchanged in this audit. These are candidate sample sizes, not fitted estimates, validated instrument strength or final approved analysis samples.</p>'''+table(main,['group','outcome','specification','eligible','outcome_observed','complete_cases','instrument_distinct','policy_regions'])+'''<p>There is observable instrument variation, but exact-sample first-stage strength, rank and regional inference must still be checked during estimation. Adding observations at a later date does not resolve few-policy-region inference.</p>''')
sec('Weekly/current-job alternative including phone respondents',table(weekly,['mode','outcome','specification','eligible','outcome_observed','complete_cases','instrument_distinct','policy_regions'])+'''<p>Combine the disjoint modes only for this separately labelled weekly/current-job outcome and common-source controls. It is a useful mode-coverage sensitivity, not a way to fill missing annual job types. In the linked non-Addis phone-only candidates, E_is has only one observed value (and one historical policy region), so a separate phone-only IV fit is not identified; combine modes for this sensitivity rather than treating the phone subgroup as its own IV experiment. If the paper’s main aim is an annual R5-to-R7 comparison, the annual in-person design should remain distinct.</p>''')
sec('Feasible next implementation','''<ol>
<li>Keep the legacy R1–R5 analysis untouched. Build a separate R7 file keyed by participant ID, with the original historic treatment/covariate lookup and an explicit interview-mode indicator.</li>
<li>Construct R7 annual salary/wage outcomes from raw annual work screens and typwrk12r7, preserving the verified legacy category and exclusion rules. Validate CAPI-prefilled records and save an outcome/missingness waterfall.</li>
<li>Reconstruct current household size from completed current rosters. For in-person observations, cross-check raw electricity, food situation, housing and asset components; use the un-suffixed R7 wi/hq version for the legacy-definition main comparison.</li>
<li>Prepare the frozen-control annual comparator and the R7-household-control annual model as distinct specifications. Current household resources may themselves respond to MTI, so the latter is a different conditional estimand; do not change their timing without documenting it.</li>
<li>Estimate each intended sample separately with exact-sample first stages and the existing few-region inference checks. Report mode/regional coverage, outcome denominators and sample counts. Historical childhood-score selection can be relaxed only as an explicitly separate sample sensitivity.</li>
<li>Build the both-mode weekly/current-job sensitivity with current size/food and historical wealth/electricity. Resolve phone-index provenance before considering a full contemporary-control both-mode model. Do not infer annual employment type from weekly type unless that equality is actually observed and confirmed.</li></ol>
<p>Neither R6 feasibility nor an entirely fresh R7 childhood battery is a prerequisite for this R7 employment extension. The lack of a new common OC maths/verbal test remains relevant only if extending cognitive outcomes, not as a general obstacle to employment estimation.</p>''')
sources=[('R5 Ethiopia questionnaire, PDF page 36, section 5.2','rawdata/yl_r5/UKDA-8357-stata/mrdoc/pdf/8357_r5_ethiopia_questionnaires.pdf#page=36'),('R7 full questionnaire, sections 1, 2 and 9.1–9.3','rawdata/yl_r7/UKDA-9538-stata/mrdoc/pdf/9538_yl_round_7_fieldwork_questionnaire_arch.pdf'),('R7 Amhara phone questionnaire','rawdata/yl_r7/UKDA-9538-stata/mrdoc/pdf/9538_yl_round_7_et_amhara_phone_survey_arch.pdf'),('TN63 wealth discussion, p.39','rawdata/yl_const_r1_r7/UKDA-9543-stata/mrdoc/pdf/9543_tn63_constructed_dataset_final.pdf#page=39')]
files=['outcome_coverage.csv','control_coverage.csv','candidate_estimation_counts.csv','roster_reconstruction_check.csv','legacy_index_definition_bridge.csv','index_provenance_checks.csv','activity_label_crosswalk.csv','production_integrity.csv']
sec('Evidence and reproduction','<ul>'+''.join('<li><a href="../../'+escape(p)+'">'+escape(t)+'</a></li>' for t,p in sources)+'''</ul><p>Raw R7 older/younger core and roster files in both modes, the constructed release and the original R5 activity metadata were inspected. All reported counts are aggregates; no participant-level dataset or contact information was exported.</p><pre>Rscript code/auxiliary/audit_r7_extension.R
python3 code/auxiliary/build_r7_reassessment_report.py</pre><ul>'''+''.join('<li><a href="'+f+'">'+f+'</a></li>' for f in files)+'''</ul><p>The candidate outcome recodes are diagnostic implementations for sample-size assessment. No new model estimates, production CSV replacements or manuscript/Overleaf writes were made.</p>''')
html='''<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Round 7 estimation extension reassessment</title><style>body{font:16px/1.55 system-ui,sans-serif;color:#223044;max-width:1400px;margin:36px auto;padding:0 24px}h1{line-height:1.2}h2{margin-top:32px}a{color:#175d8b}.finding{padding:16px 22px;background:#edf4f8;border-left:4px solid #507b98}.scroll{overflow:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse;font-size:13px;width:100%}th,td{padding:8px;border:1px solid #dbe3eb;vertical-align:top;text-align:left}th{background:#e7eff6}li{margin:8px 0}pre{overflow:auto;background:#f3f6f9;padding:16px}</style></head><body><h1>Round 7: feasibility of a consistent estimation extension</h1><p>Outcomes and contemporaneous controls · 3 November 2026 · Round 6 deferred</p>'''+''.join(parts)+'</body></html>'
(out/'r7_reassessment_report.html').write_text(html)
print(out/'r7_reassessment_report.html')
